    content: `## The short answer

If this is your first Himalayan trek, go to Everest Base Camp. If it is your second, go to Manaslu.

That is not a cop-out. The Khumbu has the best infrastructure in Nepal — the most comfortable lodges, the most bail-out points, the best helicopter coverage and a trail so well-trodden that you cannot get lost. For a first experience of high altitude, those things matter more than solitude.

Once you know how your body handles 5,000 m, Manaslu gives you something the Khumbu no longer can: an empty trail.

## Head to head

| | Everest Base Camp | Manaslu Circuit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Duration | 14 days | 14 days |
| Max altitude | 5,545 m (Kala Patthar) | 5,106 m (Larke La) |
| Difficulty | Moderate | Challenging |
| Cost (guided) | USD 1,450–2,200 | USD 1,290–1,900 |
| Access | Flight to Lukla | Jeep to Machha Khola |
| Teahouses | Best in Nepal | Basic |
| Guide required | Yes | Yes, plus two-person minimum |
| Trekkers per season | ~35,000 | ~3,500 |
| Route type | Out and back | Circuit |

## Where they genuinely differ

**Crowds.** In peak October, the Everest trail between Namche and Tengboche is a queue. Lodges fill by mid-afternoon and you will share the Kala Patthar summit at dawn with a hundred people. On Manaslu in the same month, you might see thirty other trekkers in fourteen days.

**Culture.** Manaslu wins decisively here. Because the route is a circuit that climbs from 700 m to 5,106 m, you walk through a complete cultural transition — Hindu farming villages in the lower Budhi Gandaki, then above Jagat, Tibetan Buddhist Nubri with its mani walls, gompas and Tibetan-dialect villages. The Khumbu is Sherpa throughout, and beautifully so, but the change is less dramatic.

**Reliability.** Everest depends on the Lukla flight, and Lukla flights are cancelled for weather regularly — sometimes for days. Manaslu starts with a jeep drive. If you have an inflexible flight home, that is a real consideration.

**Safety margin.** The Khumbu has the best evacuation infrastructure in Nepal, several helicopter operators and an HRA aid post at Pheriche. On Manaslu, above Samagaun, you are considerably further from help.

## Who should choose which

**Choose Everest Base Camp if** it is your first high-altitude trek, you want the iconic destination, you value comfortable lodges and hot showers, or you are travelling with someone whose altitude tolerance is unknown.

**Choose Manaslu if** you have trekked at altitude before, crowds would spoil it for you, the cultural side matters as much as the mountains, you prefer a circuit to an out-and-back, or a cancelled flight would wreck your trip.

## What most people actually do

They do Everest first, discover they like high places, and come back for Manaslu two or three years later. That is the sequence I would recommend to almost anyone.`,
